From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <bap@debian.org>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: Limit INCL nesting depth to stop stack overflow on INCL cycles

DjVuDocument::url_to_file() registers a new DjVuFile under its name
only after DjVuFile::create() returns, but when the data is already
present create() synchronously processes the file's INCL chunks.  A
cycle of INCL chunks (b includes c includes b) thus creates fresh
files forever and the recursion overflows the stack.

Upstream commit cd8b5c9 rejects a file including itself, which covers
only cycles of length one.  The Fedora patch previously carried here
(djvulibre-3.5.27-djvuport-stack-overflow.patch, for CVE-2021-3500)
remembers only the single most recent id, so it misses any cycle of
length two or more, and it keeps that id in the process-wide
DjVuPortcaster without locking.

Instead bound the per-thread INCL nesting depth.  Legitimate documents
nest INCL chunks only a couple of levels deep.

Forwarded: no
---
--- a/libdjvu/DjVuFile.cpp
+++ b/libdjvu/DjVuFile.cpp
@@ -97,6 +97,11 @@
 
 static GP<GPixmap> (*djvu_decode_codec)(ByteStream &bs)=0;
 
+#if HAVE_GCCTLS
+// Nesting depth of INCL chunk processing in this thread
+static __thread int incl_depth=0;
+#endif
+
 class ProgressByteStream : public ByteStream
 {
 public:
@@ -596,7 +601,27 @@
     GP<DjVuFile> file;
     G_TRY
     {
+#if HAVE_GCCTLS
+      // Included files are created, and process their own INCL chunks,
+      // before they can be found by name.  A cycle of INCL chunks would
+      // thus recurse until the stack overflows.
+      if (incl_depth >= 32)
+        G_THROW("DjVuFile: INCL chunks nested too deeply (corrupted file?)");
+      incl_depth++;
+      G_TRY
+      {
+        file=pcaster->id_to_file(this, incl_str);
+      }
+      G_CATCH_ALL
+      {
+        incl_depth--;
+        G_RETHROW;
+      }
+      G_ENDCATCH;
+      incl_depth--;
+#else
       file=pcaster->id_to_file(this, incl_str);
+#endif
     }
     G_CATCH(ex)
     {
